<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Q3 - Protected Route 2: Redis Session Inspection</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 30px; }
        .nav { margin-bottom: 20px; }
        .nav a { margin-right: 15px; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: none; color: #0066cc; }
        table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 680px; }
        th, td { padding: 8px; text-align: left; }
        th { background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 30%; }
        .btn-logout { background-color: #d9534f; color: white; padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 3px; text-decoration: none; }
        pre { background: #272822; color: #f8f8f2; padding: 12px; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto; width: 650px; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h2>Protected Route 2: Redis Session Store Inspection</h2>

    <div class="nav">
        <a href="/dashboard">Dashboard (Protected 1)</a> |
        <a href="/reports">Redis Session Inspection (Protected 2)</a> |
        <a href="/logout" class="btn-logout">Logout</a>
    </div>

    <table border="1">
        <tr>
            <th>User Account</th>
            <td><%= user.username %> (<%= user.fullName %>)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th>Session Cookie ID</th>
            <td><code><%= sessionId %></code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th>Key Queried in Redis</th>
            <td><code><%= redisKey %></code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th>Redis Engine</th>
            <td><%= redisMode %></td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Raw JSON Data Stored in Redis:</h3>
    <pre><%= rawRedisData ? JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(rawRedisData), null, 2) : 'No data retrieved' %></pre>

    <p><small>* Note: This demonstrates that session data is stored remotely/in-memory in Redis key-value store rather than application RAM or local disk files.</small></p>

</body>
</html>
